  "question": {
    "text": "Regular use of which of the following fertilizer increases the acidity of soil?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iVVwq",
      "text": "\nPotassium nitrate\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lWnWk",
      "text": "\nUrea\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NjEcR",
      "text": "\nSuperphosphate of lime\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KaZG4",
      "text": "\nAmmonium sulphate",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_4\\right)_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4$ is a salt of strong acid and weak base, on hydrolysis it ill produce $\\mathrm{H}^{+}$ion. This will increase the acidity of soil.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left(\\mathrm{NH}_4\\right)_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4 \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\\mathrm{SO}_4^{2-} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}+\\mathrm{H}^{+}\n\\end{aligned}$\nHence, (D) is correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
